      "Abstract": {
        "CopyrightInformation": "Copyright © 2013 Elsevier Inc. All rights reserved.",
        "AbstractText": "Shoulder pain with or without trauma is a common complaint. MRI is often the most useful imaging study for evaluating the shoulder. This review provides an overview of various modalities and their role in evaluating various clinical issues in shoulder pathologies. Imaging and arthroscopic correlation of common conditions are provided."
      },
